# The Flentrop library. The standard nine come first, numbered 0-8 as the
# tapes name them, then the 27 stops of the 1958 Flentrop in Adolphus
# Busch Hall, 9-35, a family a division, made by dacvoice from
# ../defs/flentrop/ (voices/README.md, "Stops"). The nine are the
# synthesized ones (-synth). The recorded harpsichord does not fit
# beside the stops, and the Flentrop keeps its sound.
flute-synth.voice
reed-synth.voice
plucked-bass-synth.voice
marimba-synth.voice
principal-synth.voice
gedackt-synth.voice
trumpet-synth.voice
bourdon-synth.voice
harpsichord-synth.voice

# Rugpositief (I), 9-15
flentrop/rp-holpijp-8.voice
flentrop/rp-prestant-4.voice
flentrop/rp-roerfluit-4.voice
flentrop/rp-gemshoorn-2.voice
flentrop/rp-quint-1-1-3.voice
flentrop/rp-mixtuur-ii.voice
flentrop/rp-kromhoorn-8.voice

# Hoofdwerk (II), 16-23
flentrop/hw-prestant-8.voice
flentrop/hw-roerfluit-8.voice
flentrop/hw-octaaf-4.voice
flentrop/hw-speelfluit-4.voice
flentrop/hw-nasard-2-2-3.voice
flentrop/hw-valkfluit-2.voice
flentrop/hw-terts-1-3-5.voice
flentrop/hw-mixtuur-iv.voice

# Borstwerk (III), 24-28
flentrop/bw-zingend-gedekt-8.voice
flentrop/bw-koppelfluit-4.voice
flentrop/bw-prestant-2.voice
flentrop/bw-sifflet-1.voice
flentrop/bw-regaal-8.voice

# Pedaal, 29-35. A 16-foot frame, so a part at 8 FT sounds at 16 feet.
flentrop/ped-bourdon-16.voice
flentrop/ped-prestant-8.voice
flentrop/ped-gedekt-8.voice
flentrop/ped-fluit-4.voice
flentrop/ped-mixtuur-iii.voice
flentrop/ped-fagot-16.voice
flentrop/ped-trompet-8.voice
